      "note": "NOT IMPLEMENTED -- repeated/near-duplicate invocations. Published work rates this the most frequent of 14 multi-agent failure modes (MAST FM-1.3, step repetition, 15.7% over 1600+ annotated traces), so it is the next signal to add, not one that was judged unimportant. It is deferred rather than approximated: matching on tool NAME alone would report a Bash-heavy session as one long repetition, and the command-level clustering that makes it meaningful is being built separately. Nothing partial is reported under its name."
